    "title": "Big Country braces for frigid temperatures & wintry weather - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Randy Turner ,\n58 minutes ago\nBIG COUNTRY, Texas ( KTAB/KRBC ) – Major weather changes are coming to the Big Country on Friday, including bitterly cold temperatures that will last through early next week and the high potential of wintry weather, including freezing rain, sleet and snow.\nThe Big Country’s guide to cold weather safety Before the Arctic air arrives on Friday, the weather on Thursday will be nice with highs climbing into the low 60’s. On Friday, rain is expected to develop during the day. As temperatures fall below freezing Friday evening and night, freezing rain is expected, and travel problems begin.\nThe precipitation type for Saturday and Saturday night will likely be of the frozen variety, sleet and/or freezing rain. There could also be snow on Sunday as the precipitation ends during the day on Sunday.\nWINTER STORM WATCH: Ice, extreme cold could affect travel, power, daily life this weekend Temperatures this weekend may drop to the single digits with highs in the teens. With gusty north wind, the wind chill this weekend is expected to be near zero or colder. Stay with KTAB, KRBC and BigCountryHomepage.com for updates.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KTAB - BigCountryHomepage.com.",
